decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-flat-docs
    decision: Retire the manifest concept entirely. project.atelier becomes a regular doc; empty projects are valid; sidebar is one flat DOCS group.
    rationale: 'Owner explicit feedback: ''all .atelier files should behave the same... projects probably shouldn''t have a base atelier file.'' The manifest-centric model conflated ''the canvas being edited'' with ''the project''s identity'' and produced exactly the awkward UX distinctions owner pushed back on. Pivot is mostly DELETION.'
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-docpath-required
    decision: compose-video/image/carousel helpers gain required docPath parameter (no default)
    rationale: Post-pivot, compose-* no longer assume project.atelier. Callers (createDoc, drag-drop dispatcher) compute the target slug-based path explicitly. Required-not-defaulted forces every call site to make the choice.
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-no-active-doc-persistence
    decision: Active-doc (currently-loaded .atelier) state is in-memory only; not persisted across sessions
    rationale: Owner picked 'no default — blank canvas until clicked.' Persisting active-doc would re-introduce a default on next load, contradicting that intent. Workspace-level active.yaml stays (workspace navigation) but per-project active doc is ephemeral.
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-add-slide-toolbar
    decision: + add slide button lives on the canvas/carousel-doc toolbar, not in the project sidebar's + new doc modal
    rationale: Slide-add is an action ON a carousel, not a project-level concept. Carousel docs gain the affordance when loaded. NewDocDialog drops its Add-as-slide toggle entirely — cleaner separation.
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-drag-drop-slug-target
    decision: Drag-drop ingest writes <slug>.atelier (e.g. img-7346.atelier) instead of project.atelier
    rationale: 'Multi-file drag-drop becomes natural: each file produces its own doc. Project still ends up with usable content; just multiple docs instead of one with embedded clips.'
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-listdocs-isfile
    decision: listDocs filters by statSync.isFile() AND explicitly skips basename === '.atelier'
    rationale: Defense-in-depth against the hidden .atelier/ metadata directory bug. isFile() catches the case where a fs has it as a dir; the explicit basename skip catches edge cases like symlinks. Both belt-and-braces.
learnings:
  - Owner's 'all things equal' framing is a strong simplification heuristic. When you find yourself special-casing one entity ('project.atelier is the manifest'), ask whether the special-casing is load-bearing. In this case it wasn't — the model was simpler without it.
  - 'Pivoting via team-based parallel execution scales: 13 units across 4 waves, 12 Kit spawns, all parallel where dependencies allowed. The Arky-decompose → Kit-parallel → Scribe+Rune+Aegis+Judge+Probe pattern is now the established workflow for multi-unit refactors on this project.'
  - 'Truncated subagent reports during parallel waves are common but recoverable: check workspace state directly via git status + grep + test runs rather than waiting for the verbose final report.'
  - Drifted aspect anchors are EXPECTED after multi-file refactors. paradigm_aspect_drift auto-healed 1 of 19; the remaining 18 need manual re-anchoring or retirement. This is workflow drift, not architectural drift — the aspects' CONCEPTS still hold, just the line ranges they pointed at shifted out of the smart-match window. Filing as separate Scribe sweep.
  - The 'Add as slide' UX failure was a perfect example of conflating model and affordance. Hiding a checkbox in a modal only-when-carousel makes the action discoverable to no one. Moving slide-add to a context-aware button (only-when-carousel-loaded) restored discoverability without restoring the manifest concept.
